.TH TDDA 1 "January 2026" "3.0" "tdda manual"
.SH NAME
\fBtdda\fR \- test-diven data analysis

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtdda discover\fR      Perform constraint discovery
.br
\fBtdda verify\fR        Verify data against constraints
.br
\fBtdda detect\fR        Detect failed constraints on data

.PP
\fBtdda examples\fR      Copy the example data and code
.br
\fBtdda gentest\fR       Generate a reference test "automagically"

.PP
\fBtdda diff\fR          Compare two parquet or CSV files (EXPERIMENTAL)
.br
\fBtdda serial\fR        Convert or view .serial, CSVW,
                   and Frictionless  metadata

.PP
\fBtdda version\fR       Print the TDDA version number
.br
\fBtdda help\fR          Print this help
.br
\fBtdda help COMMAND\fR  Print help on COMMAND (e.g. discover, verify)

.PP
\fBtdda test\fR          Run the tdda library's tests.

.SH OPTIONS
\fB-\fRv, \fB--version\fR       Print version number (same as tdda version)
.br
\fB-h\fR, \fB-?\fR, \fB--help\fR      Print this help

.SH SEE ALSO
rexpy(1),
tdda(3)

.PP
